# Detection: Potential Port Scan (VPC Flow Logs)
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1595 - Active Scanning / T1046 - Network Service Discovery
# Purpose: flag a source IP that got blocked while attempting many
# different destination ports in a short window -- the classic signature
# of a port scan, since normal traffic doesn't touch that many ports.
#
# Note: field/value names below (action="blocked", dest_port, src_ip,
# dest_ip) are Splunk CIM-normalized names, NOT the raw AWS VPC Flow Log
# values (ACCEPT/REJECT, dstport, srcaddr, dstaddr). The Splunk Add-on
# for AWS silently renames these at parse time -- an earlier version of
# this detection used the raw AWS names, passed a syntax check, and
# silently matched zero events until caught during manual verification.

index=aws_security sourcetype="aws:cloudwatchlogs:vpcflow" action="blocked"
| stats dc(dest_port) as unique_ports_attempted, count as attempts by src_ip, dest_ip
| where unique_ports_attempted > 15
| sort -unique_ports_attempted
